From bf268ce37000a0b03994764a9c71533b39353de4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "tom.quest session agent" <heffnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 06:23:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tom_quest: render.py reads view-spec v4
 (layers/facet-object/plot-level style)

The dashboard's view-spec moved to v4 on 2026-07-08 (app/boolback/lib/spec.ts);
render.py still read the v3 shape, so a spec copied out of the browser rendered
a figure that was not the view it came from -- and did so silently, since the
old reader has no version gate and every v4-only field is one it simply does
not look at.

Synced field for field:

  * `layers` replaces `split`. One series per layer, each with its own `facets`
    (equality) and `ranges` (numeric); a GROUP layer draws the union of its
    `members`, deduped by run identity.
  * top-level `filters` is table-only; plot equality selections live per layer.
  * top-level `ranges` is plot-level and ANDs onto every layer.
  * `facet` is a groupplot-only OBJECT: layer / param / grid / bins.
  * `size` / `opacity` plot-level multipliers and per-layer `style`
    (shape + dash) are honored, mirroring styling.ts and glyph.tsx.
  * `sorts` entries are {col, dir}, not {key, desc}.
  * `color_by` only when there is exactly one layer.
  * omitted fields take DEFAULT_PLOT's values, mirrored as literals.
  * bin edges mirror bins.ts computeBinEdges/bucketOf, keeping duplicate edges
    instead of np.unique collapsing them (which changed the bucket count and
    every label on a tied distribution).
  * a non-v4 spec now raises, as parseSpec rejects one.

The test fixture grew a per-run avg_sensitivity row: the old one carried that
metric only on a function-level row, so an avg_sensitivity-vs-asr plot pivoted
onto disjoint rows and rendered zero points -- which the non-empty-file
assertions could not see. Tests now read panel titles, series labels and
per-series point counts off the figure.

